<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tauberbischofsheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tauberbischofsheim was fought on 24 July 1866 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a>, when Prussian troops of the Army of the Main defeated the Württemberg division of the Federal VIII Army Corps at the crossing of the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tauber">Tauber</a>. It was one of the last engagements of the Main campaign, which ended with the southern German states seeking peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tauberbischofsheim.jpg" alt="Battle of Tauberbischofsheim" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilhelm Amandus Beer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beer_Bischofsheim_1866.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the war of 1866 the kingdom joined Austria and the southern German states against Prussia, and its division was defeated at <b>Tauberbischofsheim</b> in July.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg">Kingdom of Württemberg · Military</a></li></ul></section>
